            0.311
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. In a survey of 50 students, 15 students said they liked football. The number of students who like football is 15, and the (frequency/relative frequency) is (fill in the fraction or decimal)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.313,
            0.885,
            0.354
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Which of the following experiments have equally likely outcomes? Explain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.361,
            0.884,
            0.382
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) A driver attempts to start a car. The car starts or does not start."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.387,
            0.496,
            0.409
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Tossing a fair coin once."
